IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `er3-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 54, 55 and 55.01: CLAIMANTS WHO ARE INMATES OF AN
-- INSTITUTION, and CLAIMANTS (and SELF-EMPLOYED PERSONS) NOT IN CANADA.
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24 from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- These regulations take away a disentitlement that the Act would otherwise impose: s 37 of the Act (a claimant
-- who is an inmate of a prison or similar institution), s 37 again for a claimant outside Canada, and s 152.2 (the
-- self-employed person). Each rule answers whether the person "is not disentitled" by reason only of the fact;
-- TRUE means this regulation protects them, FALSE that it does not (the Act's disentitlement then stands, or another
-- provision decides). "Subject to section 18 of the Act" (availability for work, piece ei1) stays a separate
-- question: nothing here decides whether the person is capable of and available for work.
-- Out of range: ss 37 and 152.2 (the disentitlements, pieces ei2 and ei5), s 18 (ei1), s 6(1) "major attachment
-- claimant" (ei1), s 12(3) to (6) (the maximum weeks, ei1), s 10(13) and (15) (the extended benefit period, ei1),
-- s 25(1)(a), 59(b) and 63 (employment measures, ei2), ss 23(1), 23.1(2), 152.05(1), 152.06(1) (the reasons, ei1 and
-- ei5), the Canada-United States Agreement of March 6 and 12, 1942 and s 16 of the Employment and Immigration
-- Department and Commission Act (outside the texts). Each is an input.

§ `Regulation 54 -- claimants who are inmates of an institution`

-- What an inmate has been granted for the purposes of reg 54: parole, day parole, a temporary absence or a
-- certificate of availability (the last is for a claimant who is not self-employed only).
-- src:811 | 54 (1) A claimant who is not a self-employed person, who is an inmate of a prison or similar institution and who has been granted parole, day parole, temporary absence or a certificate of availability, for the purpose of seeking and accepting employment in the community, is not disentitled from receiving benefits by reason only of section 37 of the Act.
-- src:812 | (2) A self-employed person who is an inmate of a prison or similar institution and who has been granted parole, day parole or a temporary absence is not disentitled from receiving benefits by reason only of section 152.2 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 54(1), (2) (src:811-812)
DECLARE `er3 Release granted to an inmate` IS ONE OF
    `er3 release: parole`
    `er3 release: day parole`
    `er3 release: a temporary absence`
    `er3 release: a certificate of availability`
    `er3 release: none`

-- (1) A claimant who is not self-employed, who is an inmate of a prison or similar institution and who has been
-- granted parole, day parole, temporary absence or a certificate of availability, for the purpose of seeking and
-- accepting employment in the community, is not disentitled by reason only of s 37 of the Act.
-- src:811 | 54 (1) A claimant who is not a self-employed person, who is an inmate of a prison or similar institution and who has been granted parole, day parole, temporary absence or a certificate of availability, for the purpose of seeking and accepting employment in the community, is not disentitled from receiving benefits by reason only of section 37 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 54(1) (src:811)
GIVEN `the claimant is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is an inmate of a prison or similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      release IS AN `er3 Release granted to an inmate`
      `it was granted for the purpose of seeking and accepting employment in the community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 54(1) the claimant who is an inmate is not disentitled by reason only of section 37 of the Act` IF
        NOT (`the claimant is a self-employed person`)
    AND `the claimant is an inmate of a prison or similar institution`
    AND NOT (release EQUALS `er3 release: none`)
    AND `it was granted for the purpose of seeking and accepting employment in the community`

-- (2) A self-employed person who is an inmate of a prison or similar institution and who has been granted parole,
-- day parole or a temporary absence is not disentitled by reason only of s 152.2 of the Act. A certificate of
-- availability is not in the list, and no purpose is stated.
-- src:812 | (2) A self-employed person who is an inmate of a prison or similar institution and who has been granted parole, day parole or a temporary absence is not disentitled from receiving benefits by reason only of section 152.2 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 54(2) (src:812)
GIVEN `the person is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an inmate of a prison or similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      release IS AN `er3 Release granted to an inmate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 54(2) the self-employed person who is an inmate is not disentitled by reason only of section 152.2 of the Act` IF
        `the person is a self-employed person`
    AND `the person is an inmate of a prison or similar institution`
    AND (   release EQUALS `er3 release: parole`
         OR release EQUALS `er3 release: day parole`
         OR release EQUALS `er3 release: a temporary absence`)

§ `Regulation 55 -- claimants not in Canada`

-- Why the person is outside Canada, for the exceptions of 55(1) and 55.01(1).
-- src:815 | 55 (1) Subject to section 18 of the Act, a claimant who is not a self-employed person is not disentitled from receiving benefits for the reason that the claimant is outside Canada
-- src:816 | (a) for the purpose of undergoing, at a hospital, medical clinic or similar facility outside Canada, medical treatment that is not readily or immediately available in the claimant’s area of residence in Canada, if the hospital, clinic or facility is accredited to provide the medical treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada;
-- src:817 | (b) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to attend the funeral of a member of the claimant’s immediate family or of one of the following persons, namely,
-- src:818 | (i) a grandparent of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:819 | (ii) a grandchild of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:820 | (iii) the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant’s son or daughter or of the son or daughter of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:821 | (iv) the spouse or common-law partner of a child of the claimant’s father or mother or of a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant’s father or mother,
-- src:822 | (v) a child of the father or mother of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the father or mother of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:823 | (vi) an uncle or aunt of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner, and
-- src:824 | (vii) a nephew or niece of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:825 | (c) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to accompany a member of the claimant’s immediate family to a hospital, medical clinic or similar facility outside Canada for medical treatment that is not readily or immediately available in the family member’s area of residence in Canada, if the hospital, clinic or facility is accredited to provide the medical treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada;
-- src:826 | (d) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to visit a member of the claimant’s immediate family who is seriously ill or injured;
-- src:827 | (e) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to attend a bona fide job interview; or
-- src:828 | (f) for a period of not more than 14 consecutive days to conduct a bona fide job search.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(1)(a)-(f) (src:815-828)
DECLARE `er3 Purpose of a stay outside Canada` IS ONE OF
    `er3 purpose: undergoing medical treatment outside Canada`                                  -- (a)
    `er3 purpose: attending a funeral`                                                          -- (b)
    `er3 purpose: accompanying a member of the immediate family for medical treatment outside Canada` -- (c)
    `er3 purpose: visiting a member of the immediate family who is seriously ill or injured`     -- (d)
    `er3 purpose: attending a bona fide job interview`                                          -- (e), claimants only
    `er3 purpose: conducting a bona fide job search`                                            -- (f), claimants only
    `er3 purpose: some other purpose`

-- (2) The persons "considered to be members of the claimant's immediate family": (a) to (h). The relationship is
-- the enum of er3-nouns; the first nine constructors are these persons.
-- src:830 | (2) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (1.1), the following persons are considered to be members of the claimant’s immediate family:
-- src:831 | (a) the father and mother of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:832 | (b) the spouse or common-law partner of the father or mother of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:833 | (c) the foster parent of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:834 | (d) a child of the claimant’s father or mother or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant’s father or mother;
-- src:835 | (e) the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:836 | (f) a child of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:837 | (g) a ward of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner; and
-- src:838 | (h) a dependant or relative residing in the claimant’s household or a relative with whom the claimant permanently resides.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(2) (src:830-838)
GIVEN relationship IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(2) a member of the claimant's immediate family` IF
    CONSIDER relationship
    WHEN `er3 a father or mother of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er3 the spouse or common-law partner of a father or mother of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er3 a foster parent of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er3 a child of the claimant's father or mother, or of the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant's father or mother` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er3 the claimant's spouse or common-law partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er3 a child of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er3 a ward of the claimant or of the claimant's spouse or common-law partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er3 a dependant or relative residing in the claimant's household` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er3 a relative with whom the claimant permanently resides` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (1)(a) Medical treatment outside Canada that is not readily or immediately available in the claimant's area of
-- residence in Canada, at a hospital, clinic or similar facility accredited to provide it by the appropriate
-- governmental authority outside Canada. No limit of days is stated.
-- src:816 | (a) for the purpose of undergoing, at a hospital, medical clinic or similar facility outside Canada, medical treatment that is not readily or immediately available in the claimant’s area of residence in Canada, if the hospital, clinic or facility is accredited to provide the medical treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(1)(a) (src:816)
GIVEN `the purpose is to undergo medical treatment at a hospital, medical clinic or similar facility outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the treatment is not readily or immediately available in the area of residence in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility is accredited to provide the treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(1)(a) outside Canada to undergo medical treatment that is not available in Canada` IF
        `the purpose is to undergo medical treatment at a hospital, medical clinic or similar facility outside Canada`
    AND `the treatment is not readily or immediately available in the area of residence in Canada`
    AND `the facility is accredited to provide the treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada`

-- (1)(b) The funeral of a member of the immediate family or of one of the seven further persons of (i) to (vii),
-- for a period of not more than seven consecutive days.
-- src:817 | (b) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to attend the funeral of a member of the claimant’s immediate family or of one of the following persons, namely,
-- src:818 | (i) a grandparent of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:819 | (ii) a grandchild of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:820 | (iii) the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant’s son or daughter or of the son or daughter of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:821 | (iv) the spouse or common-law partner of a child of the claimant’s father or mother or of a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant’s father or mother,
-- src:822 | (v) a child of the father or mother of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the father or mother of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:823 | (vi) an uncle or aunt of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner, and
-- src:824 | (vii) a nephew or niece of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(1)(b) (src:817-824)
GIVEN relationship IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(1)(b) a person whose funeral the claimant may attend` IF
    NOT (relationship EQUALS `er3 someone else`)

-- src:817 | (b) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to attend the funeral of a member of the claimant’s immediate family or of one of the following persons, namely,
-- src:818 | (i) a grandparent of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:819 | (ii) a grandchild of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:820 | (iii) the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant’s son or daughter or of the son or daughter of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:821 | (iv) the spouse or common-law partner of a child of the claimant’s father or mother or of a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant’s father or mother,
-- src:822 | (v) a child of the father or mother of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the father or mother of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:823 | (vi) an uncle or aunt of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner, and
-- src:824 | (vii) a nephew or niece of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(1)(b) (src:817-824)
GIVEN `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` IS A NUMBER
      relationship IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(1)(b) outside Canada to attend a funeral for not more than seven consecutive days` IF
        `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` AT MOST 7
    AND `reg 55(1)(b) a person whose funeral the claimant may attend` relationship

-- (1)(c) Accompanying a member of the immediate family to a hospital, clinic or similar facility outside Canada for
-- treatment not readily or immediately available in the family member's area of residence in Canada, at an accredited
-- facility, for not more than seven consecutive days.
-- src:825 | (c) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to accompany a member of the claimant’s immediate family to a hospital, medical clinic or similar facility outside Canada for medical treatment that is not readily or immediately available in the family member’s area of residence in Canada, if the hospital, clinic or facility is accredited to provide the medical treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(1)(c) (src:825)
GIVEN `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` IS A NUMBER
      relationship IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant`
      `the treatment is not readily or immediately available in the family member's area of residence in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility is accredited to provide the treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(1)(c) outside Canada to accompany a member of the immediate family for medical treatment for not more than seven consecutive days` IF
        `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` AT MOST 7
    AND `reg 55(2) a member of the claimant's immediate family` relationship
    AND `the treatment is not readily or immediately available in the family member's area of residence in Canada`
    AND `the facility is accredited to provide the treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada`

-- (1)(d) Visiting a member of the immediate family who is seriously ill or injured, for not more than seven
-- consecutive days.
-- src:826 | (d) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to visit a member of the claimant’s immediate family who is seriously ill or injured;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(1)(d) (src:826)
GIVEN `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` IS A NUMBER
      relationship IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant`
      `the family member is seriously ill or injured` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(1)(d) outside Canada to visit a member of the immediate family who is seriously ill or injured for not more than seven consecutive days` IF
        `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` AT MOST 7
    AND `reg 55(2) a member of the claimant's immediate family` relationship
    AND `the family member is seriously ill or injured`

-- (1)(e) A bona fide job interview, not more than seven consecutive days. Whether it is bona fide is an input.
-- src:827 | (e) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to attend a bona fide job interview; or
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(1)(e) (src:827)
GIVEN `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` IS A NUMBER
      `the job interview is bona fide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(1)(e) outside Canada to attend a bona fide job interview for not more than seven consecutive days` IF
        `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` AT MOST 7
    AND `the job interview is bona fide`

-- (1)(f) A bona fide job search, not more than 14 consecutive days.
-- src:828 | (f) for a period of not more than 14 consecutive days to conduct a bona fide job search.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(1)(f) (src:828)
GIVEN `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` IS A NUMBER
      `the job search is bona fide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(1)(f) outside Canada to conduct a bona fide job search for not more than 14 consecutive days` IF
        `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` AT MOST 14
    AND `the job search is bona fide`

-- (1) A claimant who is not self-employed is not disentitled for the reason that they are outside Canada if the
-- stay is within one of (a) to (f). The purpose says which paragraph is asked; the facts each paragraph reads are
-- inputs, and a paragraph's facts are ignored for the other purposes.
-- src:815 | 55 (1) Subject to section 18 of the Act, a claimant who is not a self-employed person is not disentitled from receiving benefits for the reason that the claimant is outside Canada
-- src:816 | (a) for the purpose of undergoing, at a hospital, medical clinic or similar facility outside Canada, medical treatment that is not readily or immediately available in the claimant’s area of residence in Canada, if the hospital, clinic or facility is accredited to provide the medical treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada;
-- src:817 | (b) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to attend the funeral of a member of the claimant’s immediate family or of one of the following persons, namely,
-- src:818 | (i) a grandparent of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:819 | (ii) a grandchild of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:820 | (iii) the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant’s son or daughter or of the son or daughter of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:821 | (iv) the spouse or common-law partner of a child of the claimant’s father or mother or of a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the claimant’s father or mother,
-- src:822 | (v) a child of the father or mother of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the father or mother of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:823 | (vi) an uncle or aunt of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner, and
-- src:824 | (vii) a nephew or niece of the claimant or of the claimant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:825 | (c) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to accompany a member of the claimant’s immediate family to a hospital, medical clinic or similar facility outside Canada for medical treatment that is not readily or immediately available in the family member’s area of residence in Canada, if the hospital, clinic or facility is accredited to provide the medical treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada;
-- src:826 | (d) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to visit a member of the claimant’s immediate family who is seriously ill or injured;
-- src:827 | (e) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to attend a bona fide job interview; or
-- src:828 | (f) for a period of not more than 14 consecutive days to conduct a bona fide job search.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(1) (src:815-828)
GIVEN `the claimant is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `er3 Purpose of a stay outside Canada`
      `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` IS A NUMBER
      relationship IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant`
      `the treatment is not readily or immediately available in the area of residence in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility is accredited to provide the treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the family member is seriously ill or injured` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the job interview or job search is bona fide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(1) the claimant who is not a self-employed person is not disentitled for the reason that they are outside Canada` IF
        NOT (`the claimant is a self-employed person`)
    AND (CONSIDER purpose
         WHEN `er3 purpose: undergoing medical treatment outside Canada` THEN
             `reg 55(1)(a) outside Canada to undergo medical treatment that is not available in Canada` TRUE `the treatment is not readily or immediately available in the area of residence in Canada` `the facility is accredited to provide the treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada`
         WHEN `er3 purpose: attending a funeral` THEN
             `reg 55(1)(b) outside Canada to attend a funeral for not more than seven consecutive days` `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` relationship
         WHEN `er3 purpose: accompanying a member of the immediate family for medical treatment outside Canada` THEN
             `reg 55(1)(c) outside Canada to accompany a member of the immediate family for medical treatment for not more than seven consecutive days` `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` relationship `the treatment is not readily or immediately available in the area of residence in Canada` `the facility is accredited to provide the treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada`
         WHEN `er3 purpose: visiting a member of the immediate family who is seriously ill or injured` THEN
             `reg 55(1)(d) outside Canada to visit a member of the immediate family who is seriously ill or injured for not more than seven consecutive days` `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` relationship `the family member is seriously ill or injured`
         WHEN `er3 purpose: attending a bona fide job interview` THEN
             `reg 55(1)(e) outside Canada to attend a bona fide job interview for not more than seven consecutive days` `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` `the job interview or job search is bona fide`
         WHEN `er3 purpose: conducting a bona fide job search` THEN
             `reg 55(1)(f) outside Canada to conduct a bona fide job search for not more than 14 consecutive days` `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` `the job interview or job search is bona fide`
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- (1.1) Only the periods of (1)(b) and (1)(d) may be cumulated during a single trip, and only if the family
-- member visited under (d) is the person whose funeral is attended under (b). Such a trip may last up to the two
-- periods together (7 + 7 = 14 days); a trip combining any other purposes, or a funeral and a visit to different
-- people, may not cumulate (fork F15): NOTHING, and each purpose is judged alone.
-- src:829 | (1.1) Only the periods set out in paragraphs (1)(b) and (d) may be cumulated during a single trip outside Canada, and only if the member of the claimant’s immediate family whom the claimant visits under paragraph (1)(d) is the person whose funeral the claimant attends under paragraph (1)(b).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(1.1) (src:829)
GIVEN `the trip is for a funeral under paragraph (1)(b) and a visit under paragraph (1)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person visited is the person whose funeral is attended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 55(1.1) the most consecutive days of a single trip that cumulates the periods of paragraphs (1)(b) and (d)` IS
    IF `the trip is for a funeral under paragraph (1)(b) and a visit under paragraph (1)(d)` AND `the person visited is the person whose funeral is attended`
    THEN JUST (7 PLUS 7)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 55(3) [Repealed, SOR/2001-290, s. 3] (line 839).

-- (4) A claimant who is not self-employed is not disentitled in respect of pregnancy, the care of a child or
-- children referred to in s 23(1), the care or support of a family member referred to in s 23.1(2), of a critically
-- ill child or of a critically ill adult, or while attending a course or program referred to in s 25(1)(a), for the
-- sole reason that they are outside Canada, unless their Social Insurance Number Card or the period of validity of
-- their Social Insurance Number has expired. The reasons are the keel's `Reason for benefits`.
-- src:840 | (4) A claimant who is not a self-employed person is not disentitled from receiving benefits in respect of pregnancy, the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act, the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult or while attending a course or program of instruction or training referred to in paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act for the sole reason that the claimant is outside Canada, unless their Social Insurance Number Card or the period of validity of their Social Insurance Number has expired.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(4) (src:840)
GIVEN reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(4) the reason is one of those listed` IF
        reason EQUALS `pregnancy`
    OR reason EQUALS `caring for a new-born or adopted child`
    OR reason EQUALS `care or support of a family member`
    OR reason EQUALS `care or support of a critically ill child`
    OR reason EQUALS `care or support of a critically ill adult`

-- src:840 | (4) A claimant who is not a self-employed person is not disentitled from receiving benefits in respect of pregnancy, the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act, the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult or while attending a course or program of instruction or training referred to in paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act for the sole reason that the claimant is outside Canada, unless their Social Insurance Number Card or the period of validity of their Social Insurance Number has expired.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(4) (src:840)
GIVEN `the claimant is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
      `the claimant is attending a course or program of instruction or training referred to in paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's Social Insurance Number Card or the period of validity of their Social Insurance Number has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(4) the claimant is not disentitled for the sole reason that they are outside Canada` IF
        NOT (`the claimant is a self-employed person`)
    AND (   `reg 55(4) the reason is one of those listed` reason
         OR `the claimant is attending a course or program of instruction or training referred to in paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act`)
    AND NOT (`the claimant's Social Insurance Number Card or the period of validity of their Social Insurance Number has expired`)

-- (5) A major attachment claimant who is not self-employed and whose most recent interruption of earnings before the
-- claim is from insurable employment outside Canada is not disentitled for the sole reason that they are outside
-- Canada if (a) the benefits are for pregnancy, the care of a child, the care or support of a family member, a
-- critically ill child or adult; (b) the claimant proves they are incapable, by reason of illness, injury or
-- quarantine, of performing the duties of their regular or usual employment or of other suitable employment.
-- The text puts no connective between (a) and (b); they are two kinds of special benefit, and a claimant would
-- rarely be claiming both, so they are read as alternatives (fork F16). (b) is read as in reg 40(4): incapable of
-- both (fork F11).
-- src:841 | (5) A major attachment claimant who is not a self-employed person and whose most recent interruption of earnings before making a claim for benefits is from insurable employment outside Canada is not disentitled from receiving benefits for the sole reason that the claimant is outside Canada if
-- src:842 | (a) the benefits are in respect of pregnancy, the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act or the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult;
-- src:843 | (b) the claimant proves that they are incapable, by reason of illness, injury or quarantine, from performing the duties of their regular or usual employment or of other suitable employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(5) (src:841-843)
GIVEN `the claimant is a major attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's most recent interruption of earnings before making a claim is from insurable employment outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
      `the claimant proves they are incapable by reason of illness, injury or quarantine of performing the duties of their regular or usual employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant proves they are incapable by reason of illness, injury or quarantine of performing the duties of other suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(5) the major attachment claimant with the last interruption of earnings from insurable employment outside Canada is not disentitled for the sole reason that they are outside Canada` IF
        `the claimant is a major attachment claimant`
    AND NOT (`the claimant is a self-employed person`)
    AND `the claimant's most recent interruption of earnings before making a claim is from insurable employment outside Canada`
    AND (   `reg 55(4) the reason is one of those listed` reason
         OR (   `the claimant proves they are incapable by reason of illness, injury or quarantine of performing the duties of their regular or usual employment`
             AND `the claimant proves they are incapable by reason of illness, injury or quarantine of performing the duties of other suitable employment`))

-- (6) Subject to (7), a claimant who is not self-employed and who resides outside Canada, other than a major
-- attachment claimant under (5), is not disentitled for the sole reason of residing outside Canada if (a) they reside
-- in a state of the United States contiguous to Canada and (i) are available for work in Canada, and (ii) are able to
-- report personally at a Commission office in Canada and do so when requested; or (b) they are qualified under
-- Article VI of the Canada-United States Agreement of March 6 and 12, 1942 and reside in the District of Columbia,
-- Puerto Rico, the Virgin Islands or any state of the United States in respect of which the Commission has not
-- suspended the application of the Agreement.
-- src:845 | (a) the claimant resides temporarily or permanently in a state of the United States that is contiguous to Canada and
-- src:846 | (i) is available for work in Canada, and
-- src:847 | (ii) is able to report personally at an office of the Commission in Canada and does so when requested by the Commission; or
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(6)(a) (src:845-847)
GIVEN `the claimant resides temporarily or permanently in a state of the United States that is contiguous to Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is available for work in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is able to report personally at an office of the Commission in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant does so when requested by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(6)(a) the claimant resides in a state contiguous to Canada, is available and reports when requested` IF
        `the claimant resides temporarily or permanently in a state of the United States that is contiguous to Canada`
    AND `the claimant is available for work in Canada`
    AND `the claimant is able to report personally at an office of the Commission in Canada`
    AND `the claimant does so when requested by the Commission`

-- src:848 | (b) the claimant is qualified to receive benefits under Article VI of the Agreement between Canada and the United States respecting Unemployment Insurance, signed on March 6 and 12, 1942, and resides temporarily or permanently in one of the following places in respect of which the Commission has not, pursuant to section 16 of the Employment and Immigration Department and Commission Act, suspended the application of that Agreement, namely,
-- src:849 | (i) the District of Columbia,
-- src:850 | (ii) Puerto Rico,
-- src:851 | (iii) the Virgin Islands, or
-- src:852 | (iv) any state of the United States.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(6)(b) (src:848-852)
GIVEN `the claimant is qualified to receive benefits under Article VI of the Agreement between Canada and the United States respecting Unemployment Insurance, signed on March 6 and 12, 1942` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant resides temporarily or permanently in the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico, the Virgin Islands or a state of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has not suspended the application of that Agreement in respect of that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(6)(b) the claimant is qualified under Article VI of the Canada-United States Agreement and resides in a place where it applies` IF
        `the claimant is qualified to receive benefits under Article VI of the Agreement between Canada and the United States respecting Unemployment Insurance, signed on March 6 and 12, 1942`
    AND `the claimant resides temporarily or permanently in the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico, the Virgin Islands or a state of the United States`
    AND `the Commission has not suspended the application of that Agreement in respect of that place`

-- src:844 | (6) Subject to subsection (7), a claimant who is not a self-employed person and who resides outside Canada, other than a major attachment claimant referred to in subsection (5), is not disentitled from receiving benefits for the sole reason of their residence outside Canada if
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(6) (src:844)
GIVEN `the claimant is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant resides outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a major attachment claimant referred to in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (a) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(6) the claimant who resides outside Canada is not disentitled for the sole reason of their residence outside Canada` IF
        NOT (`the claimant is a self-employed person`)
    AND `the claimant resides outside Canada`
    AND NOT (`the claimant is a major attachment claimant referred to in subsection (5)`)
    AND (`paragraph (a) is met` OR `paragraph (b) is met`)

-- (7) The maximum number of weeks of benefits for a claimant in (5) or (6) who is not disentitled: (a) for benefits
-- for a reason in s 12(3) of the Act, the applicable number of weeks in s 12(3) to (6) (an input); (b) in any other
-- case, by the number of hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period, the table (items 1 to 41), which
-- starts at 420 hours: fewer is not covered, NOTHING. Subject to (10).
