    BRANCH
    --     item   hours in the qualifying period   weeks
           IF hours AT LEAST 420   AND hours AT MOST 454   THEN JUST 10   -- item 1: 420 - 454
           IF hours AT LEAST 455   AND hours AT MOST 489   THEN JUST 10   -- item 2: 455 - 489
           IF hours AT LEAST 490   AND hours AT MOST 524   THEN JUST 11   -- item 3: 490 - 524
           IF hours AT LEAST 525   AND hours AT MOST 559   THEN JUST 11   -- item 4: 525 - 559
           IF hours AT LEAST 560   AND hours AT MOST 594   THEN JUST 12   -- item 5: 560 - 594
           IF hours AT LEAST 595   AND hours AT MOST 629   THEN JUST 12   -- item 6: 595 - 629
           IF hours AT LEAST 630   AND hours AT MOST 664   THEN JUST 13   -- item 7: 630 - 664
           IF hours AT LEAST 665   AND hours AT MOST 699   THEN JUST 13   -- item 8: 665 - 699
           IF hours AT LEAST 700   AND hours AT MOST 734   THEN JUST 14   -- item 9: 700 - 734
           IF hours AT LEAST 735   AND hours AT MOST 769   THEN JUST 14   -- item 10: 735 - 769
           IF hours AT LEAST 770   AND hours AT MOST 804   THEN JUST 15   -- item 11: 770 - 804
           IF hours AT LEAST 805   AND hours AT MOST 839   THEN JUST 15   -- item 12: 805 - 839
           IF hours AT LEAST 840   AND hours AT MOST 874   THEN JUST 16   -- item 13: 840 - 874
           IF hours AT LEAST 875   AND hours AT MOST 909   THEN JUST 16   -- item 14: 875 - 909
           IF hours AT LEAST 910   AND hours AT MOST 944   THEN JUST 17   -- item 15: 910 - 944
           IF hours AT LEAST 945   AND hours AT MOST 979   THEN JUST 17   -- item 16: 945 - 979
           IF hours AT LEAST 980   AND hours AT MOST 1014  THEN JUST 18   -- item 17: 980 - 1014
           IF hours AT LEAST 1015  AND hours AT MOST 1049  THEN JUST 18   -- item 18: 1015 - 1049
           IF hours AT LEAST 1050  AND hours AT MOST 1084  THEN JUST 19   -- item 19: 1050 - 1084
           IF hours AT LEAST 1085  AND hours AT MOST 1119  THEN JUST 19   -- item 20: 1085 - 1119
           IF hours AT LEAST 1120  AND hours AT MOST 1154  THEN JUST 20   -- item 21: 1120 - 1154
           IF hours AT LEAST 1155  AND hours AT MOST 1189  THEN JUST 20   -- item 22: 1155 - 1189
           IF hours AT LEAST 1190  AND hours AT MOST 1224  THEN JUST 21   -- item 23: 1190 - 1224
           IF hours AT LEAST 1225  AND hours AT MOST 1259  THEN JUST 21   -- item 24: 1225 - 1259
           IF hours AT LEAST 1260  AND hours AT MOST 1294  THEN JUST 22   -- item 25: 1260 - 1294
           IF hours AT LEAST 1295  AND hours AT MOST 1329  THEN JUST 22   -- item 26: 1295 - 1329
           IF hours AT LEAST 1330  AND hours AT MOST 1364  THEN JUST 23   -- item 27: 1330 - 1364
           IF hours AT LEAST 1365  AND hours AT MOST 1399  THEN JUST 23   -- item 28: 1365 - 1399
           IF hours AT LEAST 1400  AND hours AT MOST 1434  THEN JUST 24   -- item 29: 1400 - 1434
           IF hours AT LEAST 1435  AND hours AT MOST 1469  THEN JUST 25   -- item 30: 1435 - 1469
           IF hours AT LEAST 1470  AND hours AT MOST 1504  THEN JUST 26   -- item 31: 1470 - 1504
           IF hours AT LEAST 1505  AND hours AT MOST 1539  THEN JUST 27   -- item 32: 1505 - 1539
           IF hours AT LEAST 1540  AND hours AT MOST 1574  THEN JUST 28   -- item 33: 1540 - 1574
           IF hours AT LEAST 1575  AND hours AT MOST 1609  THEN JUST 29   -- item 34: 1575 - 1609
           IF hours AT LEAST 1610  AND hours AT MOST 1644  THEN JUST 30   -- item 35: 1610 - 1644
           IF hours AT LEAST 1645  AND hours AT MOST 1679  THEN JUST 31   -- item 36: 1645 - 1679
           IF hours AT LEAST 1680  AND hours AT MOST 1714  THEN JUST 32   -- item 37: 1680 - 1714
           IF hours AT LEAST 1715  AND hours AT MOST 1749  THEN JUST 33   -- item 38: 1715 - 1749
           IF hours AT LEAST 1750  AND hours AT MOST 1784  THEN JUST 34   -- item 39: 1750 - 1784
           IF hours AT LEAST 1785  AND hours AT MOST 1819  THEN JUST 35   -- item 40: 1785 - 1819
           IF hours AT LEAST 1820                  THEN JUST 36   -- item 41: 1820 or more
           OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- fewer than 420 hours: the table does not reach it

-- src:853 | (7) Subject to subsection (10), the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period, in respect of a claimant referred to in subsections (5) and (6) who is not disentitled from receiving benefits, is
-- src:854 | (a) in the case of benefits that are paid for a reason referred to in subsection 12(3) of the Act, the applicable number of weeks referred to in subsections 12(3) to (6) of the Act; and
-- src:855 | (b) in any other case, in respect of the number of hours of insurable employment in the claimant’s qualifying period set out in column I of the table to this subsection, the corresponding number of weeks set out in column II of that table.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(7) (src:853-855)
GIVEN `the benefits are paid for a reason referred to in subsection 12(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicable number of weeks referred to in subsections 12(3) to (6) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours of insurable employment in the claimant's qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 55(7) the maximum number of weeks of benefits for a claimant not in Canada` IS
    IF `the benefits are paid for a reason referred to in subsection 12(3) of the Act`
    THEN JUST `the applicable number of weeks referred to in subsections 12(3) to (6) of the Act`
    ELSE `reg 55(7)(b) the maximum number of weeks of benefits by the hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` `the hours of insurable employment in the claimant's qualifying period`

-- (8) A claimant in (5) or (6), for whom a benefit period has been established and who then becomes resident in
-- Canada, continues to be entitled for not more than the maximum of (7): the weeks left are the maximum less the
-- weeks already paid.
-- src:900 | (8) Subject to subsection (10), a claimant referred to in subsections (5) and (6), for whom a benefit period has been established and who subsequently becomes resident in Canada, continues to be entitled to receive benefits for not more than the maximum number of weeks referred to in subsection (7).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(8) (src:900)
GIVEN `the maximum number of weeks referred to in subsection (7)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of benefits already paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 55(8) the weeks for which the claimant who becomes resident in Canada continues to be entitled` IS
    max 0 (`the maximum number of weeks referred to in subsection (7)` MINUS `the weeks of benefits already paid`)

-- (9) For a claimant with a benefit period established in Canada who then becomes a claimant of (6), the
-- maximum is the greater of (a) the weeks already received in Canada and (b) the weeks to which they would have
-- been entitled under (7) had they resided in the place in (6) when the benefit period was established.
-- src:901 | (9) Subject to subsection (10), the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period, in respect of a claimant for whom a benefit period has been established in Canada and who subsequently becomes a claimant referred to in subsection (6), is the greater of
-- src:902 | (a) the number of weeks for which the claimant has already received benefits in Canada; and
-- src:903 | (b) the number of weeks to which the claimant would have been entitled under subsection (7) if the claimant had been temporarily or permanently resident in a place referred to in subsection (6) when the benefit period was established.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(9) (src:901-903)
GIVEN `the number of weeks for which the claimant has already received benefits in Canada` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks to which the claimant would have been entitled under subsection (7) had they resided in a place referred to in subsection (6) when the benefit period was established` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 55(9) the maximum number of weeks of benefits for a claimant who becomes a claimant referred to in subsection (6)` IS
    max `the number of weeks for which the claimant has already received benefits in Canada` `the number of weeks to which the claimant would have been entitled under subsection (7) had they resided in a place referred to in subsection (6) when the benefit period was established`

-- (10) A claimant not in Canada (or one of (8)) may combine the weeks of benefits to which they are entitled, each
-- subject to its maximum in (7)(a) and (b), but not more than 50 combined weeks; if the benefit period is extended
-- under s 10(13) of the Act, the most is the maximum calculated under s 10(15) less two weeks.
-- src:904 | (10) In a claimant’s benefit period, a claimant who is not in Canada or a claimant referred to in subsection (8) may, subject to the applicable maximums set out in paragraphs (7)(a) and (b), combine weeks of benefits to which they are entitled, but the maximum number of combined weeks is 50. If the benefit period is extended under subsection 10(13) of the Act, the maximum number of combined weeks equals the maximum number of weeks calculated under subsection 10(15) of the Act less two weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(10) (src:904)
GIVEN `the benefit period is extended under subsection 10(13) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum number of weeks calculated under subsection 10(15) of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 55(10) the most weeks that may be combined` IS
    IF `the benefit period is extended under subsection 10(13) of the Act`
    THEN `the maximum number of weeks calculated under subsection 10(15) of the Act` MINUS 2
    ELSE 50

-- src:904 | (10) In a claimant’s benefit period, a claimant who is not in Canada or a claimant referred to in subsection (8) may, subject to the applicable maximums set out in paragraphs (7)(a) and (b), combine weeks of benefits to which they are entitled, but the maximum number of combined weeks is 50. If the benefit period is extended under subsection 10(13) of the Act, the maximum number of combined weeks equals the maximum number of weeks calculated under subsection 10(15) of the Act less two weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(10) (src:904)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits to which the claimant is entitled, each within its maximum in paragraph (7)(a) or (b)` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the most weeks that may be combined` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 55(10) the weeks of benefits that may be combined` IS
    min (sum `the weeks of benefits to which the claimant is entitled, each within its maximum in paragraph (7)(a) or (b)`) `the most weeks that may be combined`

-- (11) A claimant who is not self-employed is not disentitled for the sole reason that they are outside Canada if they
-- are outside Canada, with the approval of the Commission, in the course of their employment under an employment
-- support measure of paragraph 59(b) of the Act, or a measure under an agreement under s 63, established to help
-- insured participants start businesses or become self-employed.
-- src:905 | (11) A claimant who is not a self-employed person is not disentitled from receiving benefits for the sole reason that the claimant is outside Canada if the claimant is outside Canada, with the approval of the Commission, in the course of the claimant’s employment under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act — or a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act — that is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(11) (src:905)
GIVEN `the claimant is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is outside Canada with the approval of the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the course of the claimant's employment under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act, or a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(11) the claimant is not disentitled for the sole reason that they are outside Canada in the course of employment under a measure` IF
        NOT (`the claimant is a self-employed person`)
    AND `the claimant is outside Canada with the approval of the Commission`
    AND `in the course of the claimant's employment under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act, or a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act`
    AND `the measure is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed`

-- (12) A claim made for the purposes of this section is sent in an envelope or package addressed to the Commission,
-- by mail or by means of a confirmed delivery service (certified or registered mail or another delivery service that
-- provides proof of delivery, s 2(1) of the Act, in the core). (13) A claim sent in any other manner is reviewed by an
-- employee of the Commission at the time of importation.
-- src:906 | (12) Subject to subsection (13), where a claimant makes a claim for the purposes of this section, the claim shall be sent in an envelope or package addressed to the Commission, by mail or by means of a confirmed delivery service.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(12) (src:906)
GIVEN `the claim is sent in an envelope or package addressed to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent by mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent by certified mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent by another delivery service that provides proof of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(12) the claim is sent in the manner required` IF
        `the claim is sent in an envelope or package addressed to the Commission`
    AND (   `it is sent by mail`
         OR `s 2(1) confirmed delivery service` `it is sent by certified mail` `it is sent by registered mail` `it is sent by another delivery service that provides proof of delivery`)

-- src:907 | (13) Where a claim is sent by the claimant to the Commission in a manner other than the manner required by subsection (12), the claim shall be reviewed by an employee of the Commission at the time of importation.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55(13) (src:907)
GIVEN `the claim is sent in the manner required by subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55(13) the claim is reviewed by an employee of the Commission at the time of importation` IF
    NOT (`the claim is sent in the manner required by subsection (12)`)

§ `Regulation 55.01 -- self-employed persons not in Canada`

-- (1) The self-employed person is not disentitled for the reason that they are outside Canada if the stay is within
-- (a), (b), (c) or (d): the same four exceptions as 55(1)(a) to (d), with "self-employed person" in the place of
-- "claimant" (checked line by line against src:816 to 826 and src:909 to 919). Paragraphs (e) and (f) of 55(1), the job
-- interview and the job search, are not in 55.01 (finding). The rules of 55(1)(a) to (d) are called, not restated.
-- src:908 | 55.01 (1) A self-employed person is not disentitled from receiving benefits for the reason that the self-employed person is outside Canada
-- src:909 | (a) for the purpose of undergoing, at a hospital, medical clinic or similar facility outside Canada, medical treatment that is not readily or immediately available in the self-employed person’s area of residence in Canada, if the hospital, clinic or facility is accredited to provide the medical treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada;
-- src:910 | (b) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to attend the funeral of a member of the self-employed person’s immediate family or of one of the following persons, namely,
-- src:911 | (i) a grandparent of the self-employed person or of the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:912 | (ii) a grandchild of the self-employed person or of the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:913 | (iii) the spouse or common-law partner of the self-employed person’s son or daughter or of the son or daughter of the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:914 | (iv) the spouse or common-law partner of a child of the self-employed person’s father or mother or of a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the self-employed person’s father or mother,
-- src:915 | (v) a child of the father or mother of the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the father or mother of the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:916 | (vi) an uncle or aunt of the self-employed person or of the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner, and
-- src:917 | (vii) a nephew or niece of the self-employed person or of the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:918 | (c) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to accompany a member of the self-employed person’s immediate family to a hospital, medical clinic or similar facility outside Canada for medical treatment that is not readily or immediately available in the family member’s area of residence in Canada, if the hospital, clinic or facility is accredited to provide the medical treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada; or
-- src:919 | (d) for a period of not more than seven consecutive days to visit a member of the self-employed person’s immediate family who is seriously ill or injured.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55.01(1) (src:908-919)
GIVEN `the person is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `er3 Purpose of a stay outside Canada`
      `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` IS A NUMBER
      relationship IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant`
      `the treatment is not readily or immediately available in the area of residence in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility is accredited to provide the treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the family member is seriously ill or injured` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55.01(1) the self-employed person is not disentitled for the reason that they are outside Canada` IF
        `the person is a self-employed person`
    AND (CONSIDER purpose
         WHEN `er3 purpose: undergoing medical treatment outside Canada` THEN
             `reg 55(1)(a) outside Canada to undergo medical treatment that is not available in Canada` TRUE `the treatment is not readily or immediately available in the area of residence in Canada` `the facility is accredited to provide the treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada`
         WHEN `er3 purpose: attending a funeral` THEN
             `reg 55(1)(b) outside Canada to attend a funeral for not more than seven consecutive days` `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` relationship
         WHEN `er3 purpose: accompanying a member of the immediate family for medical treatment outside Canada` THEN
             `reg 55(1)(c) outside Canada to accompany a member of the immediate family for medical treatment for not more than seven consecutive days` `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` relationship `the treatment is not readily or immediately available in the area of residence in Canada` `the facility is accredited to provide the treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada`
         WHEN `er3 purpose: visiting a member of the immediate family who is seriously ill or injured` THEN
             `reg 55(1)(d) outside Canada to visit a member of the immediate family who is seriously ill or injured for not more than seven consecutive days` `the number of consecutive days outside Canada` relationship `the family member is seriously ill or injured`
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- (1.1) and (2) say, with "self-employed person" in the place of "claimant", what reg 55(1.1) and 55(2) say (checked
-- line by line against src:829 to 838 and src:920 to 929), so the rules of reg 55(1.1) and 55(2) are called.
-- src:920 | (1.1) Only the periods set out in paragraphs (1)(b) and (d) may be cumulated during a single trip outside Canada, and only if the member of the self-employed person’s immediate family whom the self-employed person visits under paragraph (1)(d) is the person whose funeral the self-employed person attends under paragraph (1)(b).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55.01(1.1) (src:920)
GIVEN `the trip is for a funeral under paragraph (1)(b) and a visit under paragraph (1)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person visited is the person whose funeral is attended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 55.01(1.1) the most consecutive days of a single trip that cumulates the periods of paragraphs (1)(b) and (d)` IS
    `reg 55(1.1) the most consecutive days of a single trip that cumulates the periods of paragraphs (1)(b) and (d)` `the trip is for a funeral under paragraph (1)(b) and a visit under paragraph (1)(d)` `the person visited is the person whose funeral is attended`

-- src:921 | (2) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (1.1), the following persons are considered to be members of the self-employed person’s immediate family:
-- src:922 | (a) the father and mother of the self-employed person or of the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:923 | (b) the spouse or common-law partner of the father or mother of the self-employed person or of the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:924 | (c) the foster parent of the self-employed person or of the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:925 | (d) a child of the self-employed person’s father or mother or a child of the spouse or common-law partner of the self-employed person’s father or mother;
-- src:926 | (e) the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:927 | (f) a child of the self-employed person or of the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:928 | (g) a ward of the self-employed person or of the self-employed person’s spouse or common-law partner; and
-- src:929 | (h) a dependant or relative residing in the self-employed person’s household or a relative with whom the self-employed person permanently resides.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55.01(2) (src:921-929)
GIVEN relationship IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55.01(2) a member of the self-employed person's immediate family` IF
    `reg 55(2) a member of the claimant's immediate family` relationship

-- (3) A self-employed person is not disentitled in respect of pregnancy, the care of a child referred to in s
-- 152.05(1), the care or support of a family member referred to in s 152.06(1), of a critically ill child or of a
-- critically ill adult, for the sole reason that they are outside Canada, unless their Social Insurance Number Card
-- or the period of validity of their Social Insurance Number has expired.
-- src:930 | (3) A self-employed person is not disentitled from receiving benefits in respect of pregnancy, the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 152.05(1) of the Act or the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult for the sole reason that the self-employed person is outside Canada, unless their Social Insurance Number Card or the period of validity of their Social Insurance Number has expired.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 55.01(3) (src:930)
GIVEN `the person is a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
      `the person's Social Insurance Number Card or the period of validity of their Social Insurance Number has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 55.01(3) the self-employed person is not disentitled for the sole reason that they are outside Canada` IF
        `the person is a self-employed person`
    AND `reg 55(4) the reason is one of those listed` reason
    AND NOT (`the person's Social Insurance Number Card or the period of validity of their Social Insurance Number has expired`)
